 "note": "Left side measured on the Getty / Sutton photo 'Andy Rouse Toyota Carina, Brands Hatch 30 June 1991' (near side-on, nose left; the model outline was traced from the same photo, so positions are read straight off it): blue top, light-blue stripe rising to the rear, red band on the front bumper top and a thin red line on the rear quarter and bumper, white lower body. KALIBER and NO ALCOHOL / NO LIMITS on the left side (the right side has ICS plc). Checked against the TV graphic drawings and the paddock photo (Super Touring Register 3371). Wheels: white 5-spoke, from the paddock photo 3371 (car standing). Uncertain: the darker navy band seen above the light-blue stripe in the Brands Hatch photo looks like shading under the body crease (it does not show in the paddock photo), so it is not drawn; small decals (Andy Rouse script, KONI/CHAMPION sizes) are approximate. Logos (2026-11-16): Shell (white), the Shell pecten, YOKOHAMA with the red Y chevron, KONI and CHAMPION are now the real logos; KALIBER, NO ALCOHOL / NO LIMITS, FUELS AND LUBRICANTS, the small driver name and the cut '...HAMA' on the front bumper corner stay text (no logo exists for Kaliber or ICS; the bumper decal wraps round the corner so a full logo would be wrong).",
